      "id": "CNT-01",
      "chapter": "global",
      "title": "The two auxiliary-prime level indices",
      "anchor": "global-count-five-index",
      "statement": "At q, the ratio of row and column indices is q^[mk+m(m−1)/2] times the product of (1−q^(−j)) over k<j≤r, r=k+m−1. Its f repetitions at each of g₀,g₁ yield the normalized leading term [m+m(m−1)/(2k)]log(g₀g₁). The remaining contribution is between −2log(2)/k and zero.",
      "hypotheses": "Finite prime fields, k≥1, even m≥2, exactly two type primes, and f>0. At the worked local example k=m=q=2 there is no claim of full family admissibility. The family has m≥44 eventually.",
      "definitions": [
        "row level",
        "column level",
        "local index",
        "free matrix positions",
        "finite general linear group"
