      "correspondence": "Count GL by independent columns and divide by each subgroup. With s=m/2−1 the formal row count s(2k+1+2s)+k(k−1)/2 equals r(r−1)/2−k. Splitting Π_r/Π_k cancels the first k factors. LinkMin weakens log(1/2) to −1 per prime. Small example: 6/2=3, 168/2=84 and their ratio is 28.",
